# Global exclusions applied when bundling templates.
#
# Patterns are matched with minimatch against the path relative to the template
# root, which means they are anchored to that root unless they say otherwise. A
# bare `.env` matches only a `.env` beside package.json; it does nothing about
# `src/.env.local`. Anything meant to apply at every depth needs an explicit
# `**/` prefix.
#
# Two classes below, deliberately:
#
#   **/  names that are unambiguously tool or developer state wherever they
#        appear. There is no template in which `node_modules` or `.env` is
#        source, so matching them at any depth cannot cost us a real file.
#
#   root names that a template could plausibly use for its own source. `config`
#        and `dist` are the obvious ones: `src/config/` is a normal thing for an
#        app to have, and excluding it recursively would silently drop it from
#        the bundle. These stay anchored to where the tooling actually writes
#        them.

# Tool and developer state, at any depth.
**/node_modules/
**/.git/
**/.rush/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
**/.rayfin-copilot.json

# Build-tool caches are unambiguously tool state under the policy above.
# `.temp` was previously anchored to `rayfin/` alone, which let
# `packages/api/.temp/` through; it is dot-prefixed tool state like the rest,
# so it is matched at any depth here and no longer listed under the root-
# anchored names below.
**/.vite/
**/.cache/
**/.tmp/
**/.temp/

# Holds registry credentials once anyone has authenticated against a private
# feed. Gitignored, so it is invisible in `git status` before a bundle is cut,
# and there is no template in which it is source.
**/.npmrc

# tsc writes `<project>.tsbuildinfo`, not `.tsbuildinfo`, so a bare extension
# never matched anything. The glob covers both spellings at any depth.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Anchored to the template root, because these names can be real source
# directories further down.
config/
config/rush-project.json
rush-logs/
dist/
build/
rayfin/.deployments.json

# Flat templates and `rayfin functions init` write these under
# `rayfin/functions`; the Universal App capability writes them under
# `packages/functions`.
# `local.settings.json` holds connection strings and whatever keys the developer
# ran with; `deploymentdata.json` holds their deployment identifiers. The sample
# gitignores both, so neither shows up in `git status` before a bundle is cut.
#
# These have to stay anchored rather than recursive: the functions capability
# ships its own seed `local.settings.json` inside
# `.agents/skills/functions-capability/kit/functions/`, and that one is source
# the scaffolded app needs. Same filename, opposite answers, so the rule is a
# path.
rayfin/functions/local.settings.json
rayfin/functions/deploymentdata.json
packages/functions/local.settings.json
packages/functions/deploymentdata.json

.templateignore
package-lock.json